# The repo root sets `* text=auto eol=lf`. That is right for the XGBoost JSON in
# here and wrong for the graphs: git's text heuristic only looks for a NUL byte
# in the first 8 kB, and a small protobuf can clear that bar, at which point a
# `0x0D 0x0A` pair occurring inside a weight would be "normalized" to `0x0A` on
# checkout. These fixtures exist to be *refused*, so a mangled one would still
# be refused — for the wrong reason, by the parse error rather than by the
# construct the test is named after, on a machine whose only sin was cloning.
*.onnx  binary
*.json  text eol=lf
